  "result": "Perfect! All 233 tests pass. The overdue report functionality is now fully implemented with 19 comprehensive tests:\n\n**Created `src/reports.js`:**\n- **`overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)`** generates overdue invoice reports\n  - Filters invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n  - Filters to only invoices with dueDate before asOf\n  - Returns array of `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }`\n  - daysOverdue = days from dueDate to asOf using daysBetween\n  - due = remaining balance using balanceDue (accounts for payments)\n  - Sorted by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n\n**Test coverage (19 new tests):**\n- Returns invoices with dueDate before asOf\n- Filters out draft invoices\n- Filters out invoices with dueDate on or after asOf\n- Includes all required fields (number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due)\n- Calculates daysOverdue correctly\n- Calculates due amount from balanceDue\n- Subtracts payments from due\n- Sorts by daysOverdue descending\n- Includes partially_paid invoices\n- Filters out paid invoices\n- Returns empty array when no overdue invoices\n- Handles multiple overdue invoices with correct sorting\n- daysOverdue is 1 when exactly 1 day overdue\n- Handles invoices with NET14, NET30, and EOM terms\n- Works with invoices having line discounts\n- Preserves invoice number, customerId, and dueDate correctly\n\nAll 233 tests pass (214 existing + 19 new).",
